            <h3 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal text-lg">Is the birth plan template PDF really free?</h3>
            <span class="text-tjb-rose-500 text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed pb-2"></p>
        </details>

        <details class="group border-b border-tjb-lavender-300/40 pb-3">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer py-2 list-none">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal text-lg">What should I put in a birth plan?</h3>
            <span class="text-tjb-rose-500 text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed pb-2">How you want labor to go, how you'll handle pain, what matters during delivery, the first hours after birth, and newborn care. A one-line flexibility statement at the top tells your team how you want decisions made if something changes.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group border-b border-tjb-lavender-300/40 pb-3">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer py-2 list-none">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal text-lg">What makes a good hospital birth plan template?</h3>
            <span class="text-tjb-rose-500 text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed pb-2">One page, short sentences, preferences grouped by the moments your nurse will manage. A plan they can scan in 30 seconds gets followed.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group border-b border-tjb-lavender-300/40 pb-3">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer py-2 list-none">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal text-lg">How long should a birth plan be?</h3>
            <span class="text-tjb-rose-500 text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed pb-2">One page. Longer plans get skimmed on a busy shift and the important lines get lost. That's why we made the one-page version. Choose what matters most and leave the rest off.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group pb-3">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer py-2 list-none">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal text-lg">When should I fill out my birth plan?</h3>
            <span class="text-tjb-rose-500 text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed pb-2">Most families start around 28 to 32 weeks, once prenatal visits get specific. Earlier is fine. Knowing your options early builds real confidence.</p>
        </details>
